@node using "Using ClassAction"


    Using ClassAction is simple. If you do not know what icon is for
    which purpose, just move the mouse over the icon and read the hint
    in the window title (you must have turned on the option ShowHelp).

    The buttons on the left are the drive buttons given in the
    tooltypes. Clicking on them will show this path in the DirList.

    In this DirList you can move as in a normal file requester.
    Special actions are available through the @{" icons at the top and
    bottom " link buttons}.
    Some of these methods can be accessed by keys, see @{" tooltypes " link Prefs}.

    After you have selected a file in the lister, you will see in the
    right listview, the file class and the corresponding defined actions.
    Just Select the action you want...

    Pressing a key will select the 1st file starting with this letter 
    also Shitf+Key will do the same for directories

    If you double-click on a file, the first defined action
    will be launched.

    ClassAction window is an AppWindow, thus you can throw icons
    on the main window .

    Start the preference program by selecting 'Preferences' from the @{" menu " link menu}.
    To quit, just click on the Close icon or select 'Quit' from the @{" menu " link menu}.

    To transform the window into an AppIcon just choose the iconify icon
    or choose 'iconify' from the @{" menu " link menu}.
    Double click on the AppIcon for the window popup.

    When ClassAction is AppIconified, you can throw icons on it so the
    file type will be recognised.
    If the class only have one defined action, it will be executed.
    Else, a window pops up with the list of all possible actions, you
    just have to choose one.


    Using the file manager is REALLY simple, the LEFT listview is ALWAYS
    the source directory and the RIGHT one on the group "manage"
    is ALWAYS the destination directory.

    With the @{" buttons below the destination lister " link buttons} you can move in this
    list and transfer files from source to destination.


    See also

    @{" ARexx Commands " link arexx}
    @{" Buttons        " link buttons}
    @{" Configuration  " link Prefs}
    @{" Menu           " link menu}

@endnode

@node buttons "The Buttons"

    @{b}Selection Buttons @{ub}

    On top of the source lister there are 6 buttons that make
    selection easier:

    All:     Select all entries in the lister, even directories.
    None:    Deselect all entries.
    Pattern: Select all files that match the pattern you enter.
             Directories will @{b}not@{ub} be selected.
    Type:    Select all files of the same class as the selected one.
             Directories will @{b}not@{ub} be selected.
    Toggle:  Switch selected/unselected entries.
             Affects also directories.
    Swap:    Swap the contents of the source and destination lister.


    @{b}Directory Buttons @{ub}

    For both listers there are buttons to move inside and create
    new drawers:

    Parent:  Go to the parent directory.
             If you are in the base directory, the list of devices
             is shown.
    Devices: Show volumes and assigns.
    MakeDir: Create a new directory; you will be asked for its name.
             If the option 'CreateIcons' is turned on, also an icon
             is created.

    @{b}Action Buttons @{ub}

    Some actions can be executed on the selected files directly by
    these buttons:

    WbInfo:  Show the Workbench icon information of the selected files.
             There you can modify tooltypes, protection bits, ...
    AddIcon: Create an icon for the selected files.
             If there already exists an icon you will be informed, and
             nothing will happen.
    Rename:  Rename the selected files.
    Delete:  Delete the selected files. You will be asked if you
             really want it.

    @{b}Transfer Buttons @{ub}

    You can transfer files with the aid of following buttons:

    Copy:    Copy the selected files to the destination directory.
    CopyAs:  Copy the selected files to the destination directory, and
             give them the name you enter.
    Move:    Move the selected files to the destination directory.
    MoveAs:  Move the selected files to the destination directory, and
             give them the name you enter.

    If files will be replaced and the option 'ConfirmReplace' is turned
    on, you will be asked if you agree.

    Some of these methods can be accessed by keys, see @{" tooltypes " link Prefs}.

@endnode

@node menu "The Menu"

    @{b}Project@{ub}

    Help:        Show this manual.
                 As alternative you can press the 'HELP' key.
    Preferences: Start ClassActionPrefs to modify the classes and
                 actions.
                 To change program settings for ClassAction, use
                 the 'Settings' menu or change the tooltypes.
    About:       Show information about the program.
    Iconify:     Close the window and create an appicon.
    Quit:        Leave the program.

    @{b}Settings@{ub}

    Snapshot Window: Save the current window position and size.
                     The next time ClassAction starts it will use these
                     dimensions. They are stored as tooltypes.

    The following options are identically to the @{" tooltypes " link Prefs}
    with the same name.
    So if you want to change one of the options permanently, you have
    to change the tooltype.

@endnode

@node infotech "Technicals Infos"


    ClassAction was first coded with DICE C 3.0 and is now developped in C++
    with StormC 3.0, using ReAction (nice name ;-).


    Miscelleaneous info :

    The prefs file is an ASCII file named : ENVARC:ClassAction/ClassAction.prefs
    The generic actions are saved in ENVARC:ClassAction/ClassAction_Gen.prefs
    The Directory actions are saved in ENVARC:ClassAction/ClassAction_Dir.prefs


    DISK libraries used if found :

        xfdmaster.library       V30+


    How ClassAction determine a class :

        1- test if the filename matches matchnames of defined classes.
        2- test if the file matches offsets of defined classes.
        3- Decrunch the file using xfdmaster.library.
        4- test if the decrunched buffer matches offsets of defined classes.
        5- test if the file is ASCII (if ASCII Offset Command exists)

        If everything fails, the file is declared as 'Unknown Class'.

@endnode


@node Install "Installation"


    To Install this stuff :


    Use the installer script given with the archive.
    To use it, just click on the install icon.


@endnode

